1
00:00:01,584 --> 00:00:03,586
[BEA] <i>I'm on my way there.</i>

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,046
<i>Wait for me, okay?</i>

3
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:10,552
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

4
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,399
<i>You know, I already pleaded with Billy.</i>

5
00:00:24,482 --> 00:00:26,860
<i>I almost begged for mercy.</i>

6
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:29,320
<i>But it did nothing.</i>

7
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:32,073
<i>That woman doesn't really care about me.</i>

8
00:00:33,616 --> 00:00:34,701
<i>What about your father?</i>

9
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:36,786
<i>He's just like her.</i>

10
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:39,539
<i>He also doesn't care about me</i>
<i>or my mother.</i>

11
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:40,832
<i>Now, Billy, on the other hand.</i>

12
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:43,918
<i>That's who he listens to.</i>
<i>Billy, Billy, Billy!</i>

13
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:46,504
<i>We need to figure out</i>

14
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:49,382
<i>how to break Mama out of that hospital.</i>

15
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,593
<i>The problem is,</i>
<i>they're about to send her back to prison.</i>

16
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:53,803
[CALOY] <i>Come here. Stop worrying about it.</i>

17
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:57,265
<i>Just relax for a while. </i>[SIGHS]

18
00:00:57,348 --> 00:00:59,309
<i>Don't worry, okay?</i>

19
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:01,186
<i>I'll take care of everything.</i>

20
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:05,273
<i>We'll break your mother out.</i>

21
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:09,194
<i>You know I'd do anything for you, right?</i>

22
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:13,615
[BILLY] <i>Dad, stop defending her.</i>

23
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:15,784
<i>You weren't there to see it for yourself.</i>

24
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:19,329
<i>Dear, why don't you go home for now?</i>

25
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:21,498
<i>Let me talk to your sister first.</i>

26
00:01:21,581 --> 00:01:24,584
[SCREEN DOOR SQUEAKS, THUDS]

27
00:01:25,668 --> 00:01:26,920
<i>Billy.</i>

28
00:01:27,003 --> 00:01:28,671
<i>Where have you been?</i>

29
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:29,839
<i>You see, Pa…</i>

30
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:32,008
<i>My former employer?</i>

31
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:34,219
<i>Well, they called me</i>
<i>to help with something.</i>

32
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:35,553
<i>Liar!</i>

33
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:37,806
<i>What's this, then?</i>
<i>Explain yourself.</i>

34
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:42,227
<i>Look at this!</i>

35
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:47,524
<i>Stay alert. We received a tip</i>
<i>from Benilda Cariño.</i>

36
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:50,235
<i>Someone might try to help</i>
<i>Mariela Mercado escape.</i>

37
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:53,530
<i>Let's search the area. You take that side.</i>

38
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:54,948
<i>- I'll take this one.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

39
00:01:55,031 --> 00:01:59,994
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

40
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:05,250
[BOTH GRUNTING]

41
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:13,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

42
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:27,564
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:37,073
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:03:40,511 --> 00:03:42,263
[STAFF MEMBER]
We'll turn her over to you, ma'am.

45
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:43,348
[OFFICER] Okay.

46
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:47,060
[DOOR CLOSES]

47
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:49,979
Don't fight back. Give me your gun.

48
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:52,523
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:53,608
Hurry!

50
00:03:53,691 --> 00:04:00,698
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

51
00:04:03,201 --> 00:04:04,410
[CALOY] Move.

52
00:04:05,828 --> 00:04:06,829
This way.

53
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:16,839
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

54
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:26,724
[BILLY] Miss, patient
Mariela Mercado, please.

55
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:29,143
She's under hospital arrest
in the psych ward here.

56
00:04:29,227 --> 00:04:33,064
Can you check if she has been transferred
or if she's still here?

57
00:04:33,147 --> 00:04:34,232
[STAFF] I'm sorry, ma'am.

58
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:37,610
We're not allowed to provide
any information at this time.

59
00:04:37,694 --> 00:04:40,863
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

60
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:43,074
Okay, thank you.

61
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:47,453
[CALOY] Move faster!

62
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,843
[CALOY] Give me your gun
and step out of the car!

63
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:10,852
Sir?

64
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,354
[TENSE STING]

65
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:14,272
Billy.

66
00:05:15,773 --> 00:05:18,526
- [LOUD THWACK]
- [CALOY GRUNTS]

67
00:05:18,609 --> 00:05:20,820
- [MARIELA SHRIEKS]
- [BILLY] No!

68
00:05:20,903 --> 00:05:22,363
- [CALOY GRUNTS]
- [BILLY] No!

69
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:24,949
[GRUNTS] Mariela, no!

70
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:27,535
- [BILLY WHIMPERING]
- [MARIELA GRUNTING]

71
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:29,954
- [MARIELA SHRIEKS]
- No!

72
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:32,790
[CALOY GRUNTS]

73
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:34,292
[GUNSHOT]

74
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:35,585
[BILLY] No…

75
00:05:35,668 --> 00:05:36,711
[CALOY GROANS]

76
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:37,795
[GUN CLATTERS]

77
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:38,796
[WHIMPERS]

78
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:41,299
- Well? Don't you dare move!
- [BILLY WHIMPERING]

79
00:05:41,382 --> 00:05:42,967
- [GUNSHOT]
- [BILLY SHRIEKS] Please.

80
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:43,968
[MARIELA] Ah!

81
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:47,847
[BILLY BREATHING SHAKILY]

82
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:50,641
Where did your courage go, huh?!

83
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:53,561
[BILLY] Stop this.

84
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:55,730
You…

85
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:58,983
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:01,736
- [BILLY WHIMPERING]
- [CALOY] Billy.

87
00:06:13,372 --> 00:06:15,666
You're the bane of our existence.

88
00:06:18,336 --> 00:06:21,380
Did you know that?!

89
00:06:21,464 --> 00:06:22,757
[BILLY WHIMPERS]

90
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:28,304
Mariela! Kill her!

91
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:31,265
[CALOY] Scared now?

92
00:06:34,685 --> 00:06:36,020
Mariela! Kill her!

93
00:06:37,313 --> 00:06:38,815
Or I'll kill her!

94
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:40,650
[BREATHES SHAKILY]

95
00:06:41,692 --> 00:06:42,944
Pull the trigger!

96
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:44,362
[BILLY BREATHING RAGGEDLY
IN FEAR]

97
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:48,950
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

98
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:53,329
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [BILLY GASPS]

99
00:06:58,626 --> 00:07:00,086
[GUNSHOT]

100
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:02,421
- [CALOY] Billy!
- [GUNSHOTS]

101
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:05,091
[WHIMPERING IN FEAR]

102
00:07:05,174 --> 00:07:10,638
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

103
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:12,098
[GUN CLATTERS]

104
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:39,292
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

105
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:49,177
Huh?

106
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,220
Huh?!

107
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:53,222
[PANICKED BREATHING]

108
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:56,225
[SOBBING]

109
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:57,810
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

110
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:04,275
- [PANICKED BREATHING]
- [CALOY GROANING]

111
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:07,987
Caloy! [PANTING]

112
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,405
- Caloy!
- Bea…

113
00:08:10,531 --> 00:08:12,241
We have to go.

114
00:08:13,242 --> 00:08:15,411
- Caloy, you got shot.
- [CALOY GROANS]

115
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:17,705
You got shot! Hey, wait…

116
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:19,081
- [GROANS]
- Caloy, wait!

117
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:21,584
- [GRUNTING] I know.
- Caloy, you were shot.

118
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:23,586
- But we have to go.
- Caloy-- How?!

119
00:08:23,669 --> 00:08:26,088
- I'll take you to the hospital.
- No.

120
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:27,673
You got shot!

121
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:29,091
- Caloy, come on.
- Don't bother!

122
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:30,384
Just get in the car.

123
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:31,928
- No, you're hurt!
- I'll drive.

124
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:33,888
- I can manage.
- Are you out of your mind?!

125
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:35,473
I said I can manage. [GRUNTS]

126
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:36,432
Caloy!

127
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:41,437
- Caloy!
- [GRUNTS SHARPLY]

128
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:43,189
[BEA] Caloy…

129
00:08:43,272 --> 00:08:44,524
[CAR ENGINE SPUTTERS ON]

130
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:50,738
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

131
00:09:01,415 --> 00:09:03,751
[PASSERBY 1]
Did you see Jake's face earlier?

132
00:09:03,834 --> 00:09:06,587
- [PASSERBY 2 CACKLES]
- I can't unsee it!

133
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:09,549
- Plus, he walks so weirdly!
- I didn't notice!

134
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,926
- That's why he slipped!
- [PASSERBY 2 LAUGHING]

135
00:09:12,009 --> 00:09:16,264
If I see him again,
I might just burst out laughing again.

136
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:18,015
You'd have slipped too
if you walked like that!

137
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:18,975
[PASSERBY 2 CACKLES]

138
00:09:20,434 --> 00:09:21,686
Caloy.

139
00:09:22,478 --> 00:09:23,771
Caloy, you need to go to the hospital.

140
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:27,066
- [GROANING SOFTLY] No.
- Caloy, you need treatment!

141
00:09:27,149 --> 00:09:29,360
- I'm okay.
- No! You're not okay!

142
00:09:29,443 --> 00:09:31,320
We need to go to the hospital!

143
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:34,699
'Bi, I'm sorry.

144
00:09:34,782 --> 00:09:36,075
[GRUNTS IN PAIN]

145
00:09:36,158 --> 00:09:37,326
Don't worry.

146
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:40,121
We'll find your mother.

147
00:09:40,204 --> 00:09:41,998
- Shh…
- Don't worry.

148
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:43,499
But Mama shot you.

149
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,126
[STUTTERING] N-No.

150
00:09:45,209 --> 00:09:46,752
She didn't mean for that to happen.

151
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:48,879
- Caloy, drive to the hospital.
- Where did she go?

152
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:51,382
You got shot.
You need to get treated, Caloy.

153
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:54,176
I'll get you out of here.

154
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:58,264
Yes, you will.
But let's go to the hospital first, okay?

155
00:09:58,347 --> 00:10:00,474
Let's-- Caloy?

156
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:03,311
Caloy? Caloy!

157
00:10:03,394 --> 00:10:04,520
Caloy!

158
00:10:05,438 --> 00:10:06,480
Caloy?

159
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:09,191
Yes, we'll get out of here. Okay, Caloy?

160
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:11,110
Caloy, Caloy, Caloy, Caloy.

161
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:13,404
Caloy. Caloy!

162
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:15,656
- [TIRES SCREECH]
- Caloy!

163
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,158
Caloy!

164
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:18,284
Caloy…

165
00:10:18,951 --> 00:10:19,869
[GASPS]

166
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:21,412
[BEA] Caloy.

167
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:22,955
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

168
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:23,998
Caloy.

169
00:10:24,081 --> 00:10:26,083
[ANXIOUS BREATHS]

170
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:29,629
Caloy.

171
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:35,551
'Bi…

172
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:38,304
Help me.

173
00:10:38,387 --> 00:10:40,139
I don't want to die.

174
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:43,351
Die? What do you mean?

175
00:10:44,018 --> 00:10:45,227
No one's going to die.

176
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:46,729
You're not going to die!

177
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:49,231
- You can't die.
- I don't want to.

178
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:50,941
You made a promise to me!

179
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:53,110
Weren't you going to take me
somewhere far away?

180
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:55,613
You were going to help me
and my mother escape, right?

181
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:58,032
So you're not allowed to die!
No one's going to die!

182
00:10:58,115 --> 00:10:59,408
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

183
00:10:59,492 --> 00:11:00,993
No one's going to die!

184
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:03,454
No one's going to die, Caloy!

185
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:05,581
No one's going to die!

186
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:11,796
If I survive…

187
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:15,633
I'll fix everything.

188
00:11:15,716 --> 00:11:17,885
Y-Yes, yes…

189
00:11:17,968 --> 00:11:20,429
- I'll change.
- You're going to live.

190
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:22,348
[STAMMERS] We'll turn our lives around.

191
00:11:22,431 --> 00:11:23,974
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

192
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:26,102
- It'll be a new day, Caloy.
- For you.

193
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:30,564
[BEA] Yes, and then we'll go far away.
We'll live a peaceful life.

194
00:11:30,648 --> 00:11:33,776
For the family we're going to have.

195
00:11:33,859 --> 00:11:35,903
[BEA] We'll do that.
We'll make it come true, Caloy.

196
00:11:35,986 --> 00:11:37,405
No one's going to die, okay?

197
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:39,240
No one's going to die! You can't leave me!

198
00:11:39,323 --> 00:11:40,741
No one's going to die!

199
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:42,034
[CALOY] Bea…

200
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:44,412
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

201
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:47,081
I love you. I love you so much.

202
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:50,084
[SOBS] I love you too! I love you too!

203
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:52,294
I love you so much!

204
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:54,380
That's why you can't die!

205
00:11:54,463 --> 00:11:56,757
Caloy! Caloy!

206
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:58,592
Caloy, I love you!
You're not going to die!

207
00:11:58,676 --> 00:12:00,803
I love you! You're not allowed to die!

208
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:01,846
Caloy!

209
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:03,681
Caloy!

210
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:05,766
Caloy!

211
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:09,478
Caloy! Caloy, Caloy!

212
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:12,523
Caloy, you can't die!

213
00:12:12,606 --> 00:12:15,109
You can't die!

214
00:12:15,693 --> 00:12:16,944
Caloy!

215
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:22,199
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
- [SOBBING]

216
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:23,576
Caloy!

217
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:25,536
Caloy, y-you can't leave me.

218
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:26,745
Don't leave me.

219
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:28,873
Caloy, I love you.

220
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:30,124
I love you.

221
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:40,134
[SOBBING CONTINUES]

222
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:43,053
I'm sorry, Caloy.

223
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:45,639
I'm sorry. Forgive me.

224
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:48,392
No… You shouldn't die.

225
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:50,186
You're not going to die.

226
00:12:50,269 --> 00:12:52,354
You're not allowed to die.

227
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:53,564
Caloy…

228
00:12:53,647 --> 00:12:56,817
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

229
00:12:56,901 --> 00:13:01,155
[SOBBING] No! You can't die, Caloy!

230
00:13:01,238 --> 00:13:04,283
Don't leave me! You're not allowed to die!

231
00:13:04,366 --> 00:13:06,702
You're not allowed to die!

232
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:09,914
[WAILING]

233
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:11,790
Caloy, please!

234
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,292
You can't die!

235
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:15,794
Caloy! Caloy!

236
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:18,464
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [SOBBING]

237
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:34,772
[WAILING]

238
00:13:34,855 --> 00:13:37,775
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

239
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:39,527
You can't die!

240
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:46,992
- [BEA CRYING]
- [CROWD MURMURING INDISTINCTLY]

241
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,244
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

242
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:51,372
[CRYING, SNIFFLING]

243
00:13:51,455 --> 00:13:53,165
- [MAN 1] Let's check it out!
- [WOMAN 1] Come on!

244
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:55,000
[INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

245
00:13:55,084 --> 00:14:01,257
[CRYING CONTINUES]

246
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:04,468
- [MAN 1] There's a man here!
- [WOMAN 1] What?

247
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:06,845
- Poor guy. He's all bloody!
- [WOMAN 2] My goodness!

248
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:09,265
- Go on, call for help!
- Don't touch him, everyone!

249
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:11,642
- [CRYING, SNIFFLING]
- [MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

250
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:13,018
[MAN 1] Call an ambulance!

251
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:14,770
- [WOMAN 3] What happened?
- [MAN 2] Call for help!

252
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:16,480
[WOMAN 1] Leave it alone! That's evidence!

253
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:22,987
[ENGINES REVVING IN DISTANCE]

254
00:14:23,070 --> 00:14:25,406
[PANICKED BREATHS]

255
00:14:25,489 --> 00:14:26,532
- [LOUD THWACK]
- [EXCLAIMS]

256
00:14:26,615 --> 00:14:27,575
[GUNSHOT]

257
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:29,285
- [BILLY GASPS, CRIES]
- [CALOY GROANS]

258
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:33,497
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

259
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:37,251
[CRYING, WAILING]

260
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:41,422
[WHIMPERS]

261
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:44,466
[TRAFFIC NOISE IN THE BACKGROUND]

262
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:49,889
[ENGINE REVVING]

263
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:53,517
[PANICKED BREATHS]

264
00:14:57,271 --> 00:14:58,856
[POLICE OFFICER] Rallo, Dela Torre.

265
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:01,150
Jomar, check what evidence
you can find over there.

266
00:15:01,233 --> 00:15:04,028
Enriquez, help the ambulance crew.

267
00:15:04,111 --> 00:15:06,906
[WOMAN 4] Looks like he escaped
using a police vehicle.

268
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:10,534
[MAN 1] Just what the heck is
going on in our town?

269
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:15,205
[POLICE OFFICER] Jomar,
see if there's any evidence.

270
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:16,874
- [MAN 1] I know.
- One incident after another.

271
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:19,460
They don't spare anyone at all.

272
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:25,424
[POLICE OFFICER]
Rallo, take a picture of this.

273
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:27,927
Document it.

274
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:34,600
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

275
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:37,436
[POLICE OFFICER]
Nothing else over there, Jomar?

276
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:43,484
[MUSIC FADES]

277
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,069
[BREATH QUIVERS]

278
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:48,781
[CRYING QUIETLY]

279
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:55,788
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" BY
SHANIAH ROLLO PLAYING]

280
00:15:55,871 --> 00:16:01,335
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

281
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:18,727
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

282
00:16:23,273 --> 00:16:24,358
[SIGHS]

283
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:28,612
[BREATH SHAKING]

284
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:30,155
- [BLADE SWISHES]
- [CALOY GRUNTS]

285
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:32,199
<i>- Come on! Come on!</i>
- [CALOY GRUNTING]

286
00:16:33,701 --> 00:16:35,077
<i>Bastards!</i>

287
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:39,081
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

288
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:41,041
<i>Help! Help! Hold on!</i>

289
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:43,168
<i>Take me to the hospital!</i>
[GRUNTS] <i>It hurts!</i>

290
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:44,837
[HORN HONKING]

291
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,422
<i>Sir, help me, please.</i>

292
00:16:47,881 --> 00:16:49,550
[CALOY GRUNTING]

293
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:50,592
<i>What happened?</i>

294
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:52,219
<i>Oh, there's blood!</i>

295
00:16:52,302 --> 00:16:54,847
<i>Sir? Hey! Are you okay?</i>

296
00:16:54,930 --> 00:16:56,140
<i>Help! Help!</i>

297
00:16:56,223 --> 00:16:57,808
<i>Oh! That looks pretty deep.</i>

298
00:16:57,891 --> 00:17:00,019
<i>What, are you all deaf? Help!</i>

299
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:01,228
<i>Tricycle!</i>

300
00:17:01,311 --> 00:17:02,855
<i>What happened to you?</i>

301
00:17:02,938 --> 00:17:04,857
<i>Oh my God!</i>
<i>Get in!</i>

302
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,316
<i>To the nearest hospital, please!</i>

303
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,484
<i>Let's go, hurry!</i>

304
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:10,487
[SOBBING]

305
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:13,490
<i>My parents disowned me.</i>

306
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:19,163
<i>But you, someone I'm not even related to…</i>

307
00:17:21,498 --> 00:17:22,958
<i>have always been by my side.</i>

308
00:17:23,792 --> 00:17:25,836
[BREATHING SHAKILY]

309
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:31,967
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

310
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:33,969
<i>What did you do, Caloy?</i>

311
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,846
<i>What's that?</i>

312
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:37,973
<i>'Bi, I love you this much.</i>

313
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:43,312
<i>'Bi, you're always by my side.</i>

314
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:45,147
<i>Everyone else has left me.</i>

315
00:17:45,230 --> 00:17:46,607
<i>I'm all alone.</i>

316
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:50,694
<i>But from now on,</i>

317
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:54,156
<i>it's going to be you and me forever, 'Bi.</i>

318
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:58,285
<i>You are permanently etched onto my heart.</i>

319
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:03,499
<i>You only called me because you need me.</i>

320
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:10,589
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

321
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:13,550
<i>Come on…</i>

322
00:18:15,427 --> 00:18:16,512
<i>You're right.</i>

323
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:18,889
<i>I need you.</i>

324
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:22,434
<i>Caloy…</i>

325
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:25,354
<i>Caloy, I need you.</i>

326
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:27,856
<i>And…</i>

327
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:33,654
<i>I love you.</i>

328
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:38,700
[SOBBING]

329
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:44,790
[BAWLING]

330
00:18:45,999 --> 00:18:52,172
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

331
00:18:55,551 --> 00:19:02,057
[BAWLING]

332
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:10,732
[BAWLING]

333
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:15,612
[MUSIC FADES]

334
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:17,865
One less person to cause trouble for us.

335
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:19,199
Caloy's gone.

336
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:23,162
Can you believe that, Auntie?

337
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:26,623
Bea's mother was the one who killed him.

338
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:32,588
When will those other two get their karma?

339
00:19:34,047 --> 00:19:35,048
It's taking forever.

340
00:19:35,132 --> 00:19:39,845
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

341
00:19:39,928 --> 00:19:41,471
Bea hasn't returned to the apartment.

342
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:43,557
Do you think something
happened to your sister?

343
00:19:45,309 --> 00:19:46,518
[CHAIR SCRAPING]

344
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:47,936
What do you think, Dad?

345
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:51,356
She's probably gone into hiding
with Mariela!

346
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:53,066
- Billy.
- Enrico.

347
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:54,693
Try calling your place first.

348
00:19:54,776 --> 00:19:56,278
Maybe she's there.

349
00:20:02,492 --> 00:20:03,660
[LINE RINGING]

350
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:05,537
Hello, Lucy?

351
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:07,331
Could I ask you a favor?

352
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:10,751
Could you check our unit
and see if Bea's there?

353
00:20:10,834 --> 00:20:12,961
[LUCY] <i>Oh, Enrico, she's not here.</i>

354
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:14,504
<i>I just stopped by not long ago.</i>

355
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:20,552
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

356
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:23,263
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

357
00:20:24,306 --> 00:20:25,557
I'm sorry, dear.

358
00:20:26,266 --> 00:20:28,560
- I never thought that…
- Never thought what?

359
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:31,188
Didn't I tell you before?

360
00:20:31,271 --> 00:20:32,481
But you wouldn't listen.

361
00:20:32,564 --> 00:20:34,691
You believed your eldest instead.

362
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:36,235
It's my fault too.

363
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:38,695
I shouldn't have kept giving in
to what you wanted.

364
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:42,449
I just hoped she might've changed.

365
00:20:42,532 --> 00:20:44,993
You don't even know Bea, Dad!

366
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:49,289
You don't even know me!

367
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:53,085
How could you possibly know
your own children?

368
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:56,880
You abandoned us, didn't you?

369
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:59,174
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

370
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:02,928
And now you want to act like
a father to all three of us?

371
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:09,101
Stop believing that woman!
We're all suffering because of her!

372
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:10,227
Billy!

373
00:21:11,311 --> 00:21:12,980
Why are you mad at Papa?!

374
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:14,523
Oliver…

375
00:21:15,774 --> 00:21:17,567
It's my fault.

376
00:21:21,238 --> 00:21:25,742
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

377
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:37,004
<i>Caloy's death…</i>

378
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,298
<i>That was Billy's fault.</i>

379
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:42,551
<i>You asked her to help</i>
<i>clear my name, right?</i>

380
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:44,177
<i>Did she grant your request?</i>

381
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:45,595
<i>No.</i>

382
00:21:45,679 --> 00:21:49,433
<i>That's why you had to ask Caloy for help.</i>

383
00:21:49,516 --> 00:21:53,061
<i>And when he was about to get me out,</i>
<i>that Billy interfered.</i>

384
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:59,443
<i>So Billy's the reason Caloy died.</i>

385
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:00,652
<i>Billy?</i>

386
00:22:02,946 --> 00:22:05,157
<i>I know you're angry about what happened.</i>

387
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:07,784
<i>But please don't</i>
<i>take it out on your father.</i>

388
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:10,871
<i>You know his condition.</i>

389
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:14,708
<i>Can you blame me, Auntie?</i>

390
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:19,254
<i>Am I always the one</i>
<i>who has to understand everyone else?</i>

391
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:23,467
<i>Billy, I understand how you feel.</i>

392
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:25,844
<i>But what's done is done.</i>

393
00:22:25,927 --> 00:22:28,972
<i>Let's just be thankful</i>
<i>that we're all safe.</i>

394
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:32,017
<i>For how long?</i>

395
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:33,935
<i>Pa, I'm turning myself in.</i>

396
00:22:34,019 --> 00:22:37,939
<i>I'll also surrender Mama</i>
<i>if it'll bring peace to everyone.</i>

397
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:41,276
<i>Pa…</i>

398
00:22:42,944 --> 00:22:45,197
<i>- Pa, I'm really sorry.</i>
<i>- You traitor!</i>

399
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:51,912
<i>You promised I'd be free,</i>
<i>and now you're taking it back?</i>

400
00:22:51,995 --> 00:22:53,872
<i>Bea? Bea!</i>

401
00:22:53,955 --> 00:22:56,083
<i>I won't let you!</i>

402
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:57,167
<i>Ma!</i>

403
00:22:58,502 --> 00:22:59,544
<i>Ma!</i>

404
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:01,046
<i>Bea!</i>

405
00:23:03,173 --> 00:23:04,216
<i>Ma!</i>
